                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+space"}> Compactly generated spaces
                , and likewise based compactly generated spaces, with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                the surjections and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                the subspace inclusions. The point is an
                = succeed "-generator." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi E
                        %mo ,
                        %mi M
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E,M)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-topological+space"}> Quasi-topological spaces
                \. Note that this category is not
                = succeed "-well-copowered." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Banach+spaces"} Banach spaces
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                the epimorphisms, equivalently the dense maps, and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extremal+monomorphisms"} extremal monomorphisms
                = succeed "-generator." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi E
                        %mo ,
                        %mi M
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E,M)
          %h2#related_notions Related notions
          %p
            The term
            %strong locally ranked
            is sometimes used to refer to a locally bounded category which in addition is co-wellpowered. For example, this terminology is used in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#AHRT"} Adámek et. al.
          %h2#references References
          %p The contents of this page are taken from:
          %ul#KellyLack
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Max+Kelly"}> Max Kelly
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steve+Lack"} Steve Lack
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                \-cat is locally presentable or locally bounded if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                is so
              TAC (2001)
